1. DEFINITIONS

"Aerolynq Module" means a WiFi/Bluetooth combo module designed, branded and
sold by Aerolynq that is based on Infineon (including former Cypress) WiFi
and Bluetooth chips, including the CYWL6208, CYWL6209, CYWL6302, CYWL6305 and
CYWL6612, and any later module that Aerolynq identifies as supported.

"Authorized Module" means a genuine Aerolynq Module that was obtained from
Aerolynq or from a distributor authorized by Aerolynq.

"Product" means a hardware product or system that contains an Authorized
Module and runs the Software, or a binary build of it.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software, or of a Product containing
it, in connection with a sale, lease, license or other supply for
consideration, or in mass production, or otherwise for the business
purposes of an organization. Evaluation, development, prototyping,
teaching, academic research and personal non-commercial projects are not
Commercial Use.

"Commercial Authorization" means a written authorization from Aerolynq for
Commercial Use, as described in Section 3.

"Derivative Work" means any modification of, addition to, or work based on
the Software, including a port to other hardware or another operating
system.

"Third-Party Component" means any file or binary in or used with the
Package that is not owned by Aerolynq, as described in Section 7.

